course: dictionary
lesson: 14315
title: The word obligation
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An obligation is something you must do. Someone has set it, such as a rule, a promise or your duty. «Ravi had an obligation to feed the class rabbit every morning.» Ravi is not free to choose. The rule says he must do it.
explain: Obligation can also be a feeling. «Sam felt a sense of obligation to help his neighbour, who had helped him when his bike broke.» Sam feels he ought to help, even though no one is making him. He wants to pay back the kindness.
explain: In writing, you may see «no obligation» in a shop advert. «Free quote, no obligation» means you do not have to buy anything or agree to anything. To check the meaning, put your idea in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: An obligation is something you must do because of a rule, a promise or a duty.
fact: The feeling that you ought to do something, such as helping someone who helped you, is also called an obligation.
fact: «No obligation» means you do not have to buy or agree to anything.
fact: «Under an obligation» means you have to do something, usually because you promised or agreed.
fact: In official writing, an obligation is a duty set by law or by a contract.
exercise: «Ravi had an obligation to feed the class rabbit every morning.» What is an obligation? | *Something you must do because of a rule, promise or duty | A fancy new toy | Something you may do if you feel like it | A type of weather
exercise: A shop advert says «Free quote, no obligation.» What does no obligation mean? | You have to pay later | *You do not have to buy or agree | You must buy two | You must come back tomorrow
exercise: «Sam felt a sense of obligation to help his neighbour, who had helped him.» Which word tells us Sam felt he ought to help? | helped | Sam | neighbour | *obligation
test: «The law places an obligation on drivers to wear seatbelts.» What does this tell us? | *Drivers must wear seatbelts by law | Seatbelts are sold in shops | Drivers should buy new cars | Drivers can wear seatbelts if they like
test: «Dad said we had a family obligation to tidy up after dinner.» What does obligation mean here? | *A duty we must do | A place to visit | A nice surprise | A game we play
exam: «Maya made a promise, so she felt under an obligation to keep it.» What does under an obligation mean? | She was very tired | She could choose to keep it or not | She forgot about it | *She had to keep it because of her promise
